FastAPI GET & POST Endpoints: Building Your First AI Request API
Week 2 · Day 10 of 45
Hands-on development
Today, you'll move beyond simple FastAPI routes and build the first working version of your AI Platform Gateway API.
By the end of this lesson, your application will support:
1.	Listing available AI models.
2.	Retrieving details of a specific model.
3.	Submitting an AI request using POST /requests.
4.	Accepting and validating JSON request bodies.
5.	Returning structured JSON responses.
1. Understand GET vs POST
An API endpoint is a URL through which another application communicates with your backend.
Method	Purpose	Example
GET	Retrieve information	GET /models
GET	Retrieve one model	GET /models/gpt-4o
POST	Submit information	POST /requests
Example: GET request
When a user opens:
GET /models
Your API returns available AI models.
Example: POST request
When a user submits a prompt:
POST /requests
The API receives JSON data in the request body:
JSON
{
    "model": "gpt-4o",
    "prompt": "Explain Retrieval Augmented Generation",
    "max_tokens": 500
}

Your backend processes the request and returns a JSON response.
Remember: GET generally retrieves data. POST submits data for processing or creation.
