}
Click Execute.
Your response should look similar to this:
JSON
{
    "request_id": "req_a1b2c3d4",
    "model": "gpt-4o",
    "status": "success",
    "input_tokens": 4,
    "output_tokens": 6,
    "total_tokens": 10,
    "message": "AI request processed successfully (simulation)"
}
The request ID will be different each time.
Understand the complete POST workflow
 
This separation between API routes, schemas and business logic is an important backend engineering practice.
8. Test error scenarios
Don't test only successful requests. A production-oriented engineer also tests invalid input.
Try these requests in Swagger.
Test A — Invalid model
JSON
{
    "model": "invalid-model",
    "prompt": "Explain AI",
    "max_tokens": 100
}
Expected: 404 Not Found.
Test B — Empty prompt
JSON
{
    "model": "gpt-4o",
    "prompt": "",
    "max_tokens": 100
}
Expected: 422 Unprocessable Entity, because the prompt must contain at least one character.
Test C — Invalid token limit
JSON
{
    "model": "gpt-4o",
    "prompt": "Explain AI",
    "max_tokens": 5000
}
Expected: 422 Unprocessable Entity, because model is required.
9. Understand the HTTP status codes
Status	Meaning	Our example
200	OK	GET model list
201	Created	Commonly used when creating a resource
404	Not Found	Invalid model ID
422	Validation error	Empty prompt or invalid token limit
500	Internal Server Error	Unexpected backend failure
Note: Our POST endpoint currently returns 200. In a later improvement, when we treat the request as a newly created resource, we can return 201.
10. Interview preparation
Study these questions and practise answering them aloud.
Q1. What is the difference between GET and POST?
GET retrieves information from a server. POST sends data to a server for processing or resource creation.
Q2. What is a request body in FastAPI?
A request body contains data sent by a client, usually in JSON format. FastAPI can validate that data using Pydantic models.
Q3. What is Pydantic?
Pydantic is a Python library used for data validation and serialization. FastAPI uses Pydantic models to validate request bodies and structure responses.
Q4. What is APIRouter?
APIRouter helps organize API endpoints into separate modules, making a FastAPI project easier to maintain and scale.
Q5. What is the difference between 404 and 422?
•	404 means the requested resource could not be found.
•	422 means the request data failed validation.
Q6. Why should business logic be separated from API endpoints?
It improves maintainability, reusability, testing and separation of responsibilities. API routes handle HTTP communication, while services handle application logic.
11. Today's coding exercises
Complete these independently without copying the existing endpoint code.
Exercise 1 — Add a model count endpoint
Create:
GET /models/count
Expected response:
{
    "total_models": 3
}
Exercise 2 — Add a provider filter
Create:
GET /models/provider/OpenAI
Expected response: only models belonging to OpenAI.
Hint: Use a loop over AVAILABLE_MODELS.values() and filter by provider.
Exercise 3 — Add a prompt length endpoint
Create:
POST /requests/validate
Accept:
JSON
{
    "prompt": "Explain AI Platform Engineering"
}
Return:
JSON
{
    "valid": true,
    "prompt_length": 32
}
Hint: Create a new Pydantic request schema and use Python's len() function.
